**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The domain name or IP address to query.'}, 'record_type': {'anyOf': [{'enum': ['A', 'AAAA', 'MX', 'NS', 'SRV', 'TXT', 'PTR'], 'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "DNS record type (e.g., 'A', 'AAAA', 'MX', 'NS', 'SRV', 'TXT', 'PTR')."}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Additional arguments for nslookup. (e.g. '_ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs.corp.local' or '_kerberos._tcp.dc._msdcs.corp.local')"}, 'timeout': {'default': 60, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum execution time in seconds.'}}, 'required': ['query'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_kerbrute
### Description: Run kerbrute for Kerberos-based user enumeration and password spraying.
Modes:
    - 'userenum'     : Enumerate valid usernames. This does not cause any login failures so it will not lock out any accounts.
    - 'passwordspray': Spray a single password against many users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
    - 'bruteforce'   : Bruteforce passwords for users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'domain': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Target domain (e.g., 'corp.local')."}, 'dc_ip': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Domain controller IP address. If blank, will lookup via DNS.'}, 'mode': {'enum': ['userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce'], 'type': 'string', 'description': "Kerbrute mode ('userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce')."}, 'usersfile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Path to file containing usernames.'}, 'bruteforcefile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Path to file containing username and password combinations (for bruteforce) in the format 'username:password'."}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Single password (for passwordspray).'}, 'safe': {'default': False, 'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Enable safe mode (avoid account lockouts). When this option is enabled, if an account comes back as locked out, it will abort all threads to stop locking out any other accounts. Default: False.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional kerbrute arguments.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 300, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds. Default: 300 seconds.'}}, 'required': ['domain', 'dc_ip', 'mode'], 'type': 'object'}```

